# CR 602.2a: activating an ability from a hidden zone reveals the card that has it, as the ability is announced and put on
# the stack - one event (the lasting reveal of CR 701.20a is RX-7, docs/rules-exceptions.md). Urban Retreat's "{2}, Return a tapped
# creature you control to its owner's hand: Put this card from your hand onto the battlefield" keeps the card in the hand
# while the ability waits on the stack. The reveal is made as the activation is committed, once nothing more may give it up
# (the owner's ruling of 2026-11-21, docs/engine-design.md "Taking back an illegal action"): before the activation nothing has been revealed, nor while the cost asks which
# tapped creature to return; once the cost is paid, with the ability on the stack and the card still in the hand, it has
# been revealed by Bot1 once. Bot1's Ornithopter attacks on turn 3 to be tapped, and the Moxen pay the {2}.

[Bot1 Deck]
Ornithopter
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Urban Retreat
Plains
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Revealed = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Urban Retreat.Activate
? Bot1.Revealed = (absent)
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
? Stack = Urban Retreat
? Bot1.Hand = Ornithopter; Plains; Plains; Plains; Plains; Urban Retreat
? Bot1.Revealed = Urban Retreat

[Expect]
Bot1.Revealed = Urban Retreat
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Pearl; Mox Jet; Urban Retreat
Bot2.Revealed = (absent)
